{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":" creates an app-specific table factory. Use it to define shared features, row models, and default table options once, then create each Angular table with the columns and data that are unique to that table."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same API can also register reusable table, cell, and header components, but component registration is optional. Start with shared options and features first; add reusable components only when your app needs standardized table UI pieces."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../examples/basic-app-table","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic App Table"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Minimal "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":" usage without the larger component registry."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../examples/composable-tables","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Composable Tables"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Richer Users and Products tables sharing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/app/table.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" and reusable components."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"start-with-shared-features-and-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Start With Shared Features and Options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create one app table hook and put the feature set, row models, and shared defaults there. This example makes sorting available to every table created by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectAppTable"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createTableHook,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortFns,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  sortFns,\n})\n\nconst { injectAppTable, createAppColumnHelper } = createTableHook({\n  features,\n  debugTable: true,\n  enableSortingRemoval: false,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options passed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":" become defaults for every table created by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectAppTable"},{"type":"text","value":". The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"features"},{"type":"text","value":" option is also bound to the returned column helper, so column definitions know that sorting APIs are available."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"create-app-columns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create App Columns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create one column helper per row type. The helper is already bound to your app's feature set, so each table does not need to thread "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"typeof features"},{"type":"text","value":" through its column definitions."}]},{"type":"code","value":"type Person = {\n  firstName: string\n  lastName: string\n  age: number\n  visits: number\n}\n\nconst columnHelper = createAppColumnHelper<Person>()\n\nconst columns = columnHelper.columns([\n  columnHelper.accessor('firstName', {\n    cell: (info) => info.getValue(),\n  }),\n  columnHelper.accessor((row) => row.lastName, {\n    id: 'lastName',\n    header: () => 'Last Name',\n    cell: (info) => info.getValue(),\n  }),\n  columnHelper.accessor('age', {\n    header: 'Age',\n  }),\n  columnHelper.accessor('visits', {\n    header: 'Visits',\n  }),\n])","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"create-a-table","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create A Table"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create each table with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectAppTable"},{"type":"text","value":". The call site provides table-specific inputs such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columns"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":"; shared features and defaults come from the hook."}]},{"type":"code","value":"export class UsersTable {\n  readonly data = signal<Array<Person>>([])\n\n  readonly table = injectAppTable(() => ({\n    key: 'users-table',\n    columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n  }))\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"render-with-the-normal-table-apis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Render With The Normal Table APIs"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can render the table with the same table instance APIs used by a standalone "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectTable"},{"type":"text","value":" table. This simple path does not require "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"appCell"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"appHeader"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"appFooter"},{"type":"text","value":", or registered components."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<table>\n  <thead>\n    @for (headerGroup of table.getHeaderGroups(); track headerGroup.id) {\n    <tr>\n      @for (header of headerGroup.headers; track header.id) {\n      <th (click)=\"header.column.getToggleSortingHandler()?.($event)\">\n        @if (!header.isPlaceholder) {\n        <ng-container *flexRenderHeader=\"header; let headerCell\">\n          {{ headerCell }}\n        </ng-container>\n        }\n      </th>\n      }\n    </tr>\n    }\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    @for (row of table.getRowModel().rows; track row.id) {\n    <tr>\n      @for (cell of row.getAllCells(); track cell.id) {\n      <td>\n        <ng-container *flexRenderCell=\"cell; let renderCell\">\n          {{ renderCell }}\n        </ng-container>\n      </td>\n      }\n    </tr>\n    }\n  </tbody>\n</table>","lang":"html"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"override-shared-defaults-per-table","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Override Shared Defaults Per Table"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options passed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectAppTable"},{"type":"text","value":" override defaults from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":". Use this for the few tables that need different behavior without creating a separate app hook."}]},{"type":"code","value":"readonly table = injectAppTable(() => ({\n  key: 'sortable-users-table',\n  columns,\n  data: this.data(),\n  enableSortingRemoval: true,\n}))","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"optional-reusable-components","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional: Reusable Components"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The richer composable-tables example also uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":" as a component registry. Use this when several tables should share the same toolbar controls, cell renderers, header renderers, or footer renderers."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"component-registry-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Component Registry Setup"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The composable tables example keeps the shared setup in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/app/table.ts"},{"type":"text","value":". That file creates one app-specific table factory and exports the helpers used by the rest of the example."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  createFilteredRowModel,\n  createPaginatedRowModel,\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createTableHook,\n  filterFns,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortFns,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nimport {\n  PaginationControls,\n  RowCount,\n  TableToolbar,\n} from './components/table-components'\nimport {\n  CategoryCell,\n  NumberCell,\n  PriceCell,\n  ProgressCell,\n  RowActionsCell,\n  StatusCell,\n  TextCell,\n} from './components/cell-components'\nimport {\n  ColumnFilter,\n  FooterColumnId,\n  FooterSum,\n  SortIndicator,\n} from './components/header-components'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel(),\n  paginatedRowModel: createPaginatedRowModel(),\n  sortFns,\n  filterFns,\n})\n\nexport const {\n  createAppColumnHelper,\n  injectAppTable,\n  injectTableContext,\n  injectTableCellContext,\n  injectTableHeaderContext,\n} = createTableHook({\n  features,\n  getRowId: (row) => row.id,\n  tableComponents: {\n    PaginationControls,\n    RowCount,\n    TableToolbar,\n  },\n  cellComponents: {\n    TextCell,\n    NumberCell,\n    ProgressCell,\n    StatusCell,\n    CategoryCell,\n    PriceCell,\n    RowActionsCell,\n  },\n  headerComponents: {\n    SortIndicator,\n    ColumnFilter,\n    FooterColumnId,\n    FooterSum,\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This file is the source of truth for the feature set, row model pipeline, row IDs, and registered components used by both tables in the example."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"returned-helpers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returned Helpers"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Helper"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Purpose"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectAppTable"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a table with the app's shared "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"features"},{"type":"text","value":" (including row model factories), defaults, and registered components already attached."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAppColumnHelper"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates column helpers where "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"footer"},{"type":"text","value":" contexts know about the registered components."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectTableContext"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reads the current table inside registered table components like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PaginationControls"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectTableCellContext"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reads the current cell inside registered cell components like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TextCell"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectTableHeaderContext"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reads the current header/footer inside registered header components like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SortIndicator"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"component-columns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Component Columns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAppColumnHelper<TData>()"},{"type":"text","value":" instead of the base column helper when column definitions should render registered components."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { flexRenderComponent } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\nimport { createAppColumnHelper } from '../../table'\nimport type { Person } from '../../makeData'\n\nconst personColumnHelper = createAppColumnHelper<Person>()\n\nreadonly columns = personColumnHelper.columns([\n  personColumnHelper.accessor('firstName', {\n    header: 'First Name',\n    footer: ({ header }) => flexRenderComponent(header.FooterColumnId),\n    cell: ({ cell }) => flexRenderComponent(cell.TextCell),\n  }),\n  personColumnHelper.accessor('age', {\n    header: 'Age',\n    footer: ({ header }) => flexRenderComponent(header.FooterSum),\n    cell: ({ cell }) => flexRenderComponent(cell.NumberCell),\n  }),\n])","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The registered components are available through the enhanced "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header"},{"type":"text","value":" objects because the column helper is bound to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":" configuration."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"component-table-rendering","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Component Table Rendering"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create each table with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectAppTable"},{"type":"text","value":". Per-table options provide the data and columns; shared features and row models come from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/app/table.ts"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"table = injectAppTable(() => ({\n  key: 'users-table',\n  columns: this.columns,\n  data: this.data(),\n  debugTable: true,\n}))","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Angular table instance is augmented with:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.PaginationControls"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.RowCount"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.TableToolbar"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.appCell(cell)"},{"type":"text","value":" for enhanced cell component types in templates"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.appHeader(header)"},{"type":"text","value":" for enhanced header component types in templates"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.appFooter(footer)"},{"type":"text","value":" for enhanced footer component types in templates"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Registered table components can access the table through Angular DI:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export class PaginationControls {\n  readonly table = injectTableContext()\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In templates, use the Angular rendering helpers with the app wrappers:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"@for (_header of headerGroup.headers; track _header.id) { @let header =\ntable.appHeader(_header);\n\n<th (click)=\"header.column.getToggleSortingHandler()?.($event)\">\n  <ng-container *flexRenderHeader=\"header; let value\">\n    {{ value }}\n  </ng-container>\n  <ng-container\n    *flexRender=\"header.SortIndicator; props: header.getContext(); let value\"\n  >\n    {{ value }}\n  </ng-container>\n</th>\n}","lang":"html"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"reusing-the-component-registry","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reusing The Component Registry"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The example has separate Users and Products table components. Both import "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAppColumnHelper"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectAppTable"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/app/table.ts"},{"type":"text","value":", so they share sorting, filtering, pagination, row IDs, toolbar controls, cell renderers, and header/footer renderers while keeping their own data and columns."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If different product areas need incompatible defaults, create another "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":" setup file and export a second set of app helpers from there."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"when-to-use-this-pattern","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When To Use This Pattern"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":" when multiple tables should share features, row models, default options, or conventions. Use the standalone "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectTable"},{"type":"text","value":" API for a one-off table. Add the component registry only when the app wants standardized reusable table UI pieces."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2},{"id":"start-with-shared-features-and-options","text":"Start With Shared Features and Options","level":2},{"id":"create-app-columns","text":"Create App Columns","level":2},{"id":"create-a-table","text":"Create A Table","level":2},{"id":"render-with-the-normal-table-apis","text":"Render With The Normal Table APIs","level":2},{"id":"override-shared-defaults-per-table","text":"Override Shared Defaults Per Table","level":2},{"id":"optional-reusable-components","text":"Optional: Reusable Components","level":2},{"id":"component-registry-setup","text":"Component Registry Setup","level":3},{"id":"returned-helpers","text":"Returned Helpers","level":3},{"id":"component-columns","text":"Component Columns","level":3},{"id":"component-table-rendering","text":"Component Table Rendering","level":3},{"id":"reusing-the-component-registry","text":"Reusing The Component Registry","level":3},{"id":"when-to-use-this-pattern","text":"When To Use This Pattern","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n`createTableHook` creates an app-specific table factory. Use it to define shared features, row models, and default table options once, then create each Angular table with the columns and data that are unique to that table.\n\nThe same API can also register reusable table, cell, and header components, but component registration is optional. Start with shared options and features first; add reusable components only when your app needs standardized table UI pieces.\n\n## Examples\n\n- [Basic App Table](../examples/basic-app-table) - Minimal `createTableHook` usage without the larger component registry.\n- [Composable Tables](../examples/composable-tables) - Richer Users and Products tables sharing `src/app/table.ts` and reusable components.\n\n## Start With Shared Features and Options\n\nCreate one app table hook and put the feature set, row models, and shared defaults there. This example makes sorting available to every table created by `injectAppTable`.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createTableHook,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortFns,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  sortFns,\n})\n\nconst { injectAppTable, createAppColumnHelper } = createTableHook({\n  features,\n  debugTable: true,\n  enableSortingRemoval: false,\n})\n```\n\nOptions passed to `createTableHook` become defaults for every table created by `injectAppTable`. The `features` option is also bound to the returned column helper, so column definitions know that sorting APIs are available.\n\n## Create App Columns\n\nCreate one column helper per row type. The helper is already bound to your app's feature set, so each table does not need to thread `typeof features` through its column definitions.\n\n```ts\ntype Person = {\n  firstName: string\n  lastName: string\n  age: number\n  visits: number\n}\n\nconst columnHelper = createAppColumnHelper<Person>()\n\nconst columns = columnHelper.columns([\n  columnHelper.accessor('firstName', {\n    cell: (info) => info.getValue(),\n  }),\n  columnHelper.accessor((row) => row.lastName, {\n    id: 'lastName',\n    header: () => 'Last Name',\n    cell: (info) => info.getValue(),\n  }),\n  columnHelper.accessor('age', {\n    header: 'Age',\n  }),\n  columnHelper.accessor('visits', {\n    header: 'Visits',\n  }),\n])\n```\n\n## Create A Table\n\nCreate each table with `injectAppTable`. The call site provides table-specific inputs such as `columns` and `data`; shared features and defaults come from the hook.\n\n```ts\nexport class UsersTable {\n  readonly data = signal<Array<Person>>([])\n\n  readonly table = injectAppTable(() => ({\n    key: 'users-table',\n    columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n  }))\n}\n```\n\n## Render With The Normal Table APIs\n\nYou can render the table with the same table instance APIs used by a standalone `injectTable` table. This simple path does not require `appCell`, `appHeader`, `appFooter`, or registered components.\n\n```html\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    @for (headerGroup of table.getHeaderGroups(); track headerGroup.id) {\n    <tr>\n      @for (header of headerGroup.headers; track header.id) {\n      <th (click)=\"header.column.getToggleSortingHandler()?.($event)\">\n        @if (!header.isPlaceholder) {\n        <ng-container *flexRenderHeader=\"header; let headerCell\">\n          {{ headerCell }}\n        </ng-container>\n        }\n      </th>\n      }\n    </tr>\n    }\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    @for (row of table.getRowModel().rows; track row.id) {\n    <tr>\n      @for (cell of row.getAllCells(); track cell.id) {\n      <td>\n        <ng-container *flexRenderCell=\"cell; let renderCell\">\n          {{ renderCell }}\n        </ng-container>\n      </td>\n      }\n    </tr>\n    }\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n```\n\n## Override Shared Defaults Per Table\n\nOptions passed to `injectAppTable` override defaults from `createTableHook`. Use this for the few tables that need different behavior without creating a separate app hook.\n\n```ts\nreadonly table = injectAppTable(() => ({\n  key: 'sortable-users-table',\n  columns,\n  data: this.data(),\n  enableSortingRemoval: true,\n}))\n```\n\n## Optional: Reusable Components\n\nThe richer composable-tables example also uses `createTableHook` as a component registry. Use this when several tables should share the same toolbar controls, cell renderers, header renderers, or footer renderers.\n\n### Component Registry Setup\n\nThe composable tables example keeps the shared setup in `src/app/table.ts`. That file creates one app-specific table factory and exports the helpers used by the rest of the example.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  createFilteredRowModel,\n  createPaginatedRowModel,\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createTableHook,\n  filterFns,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortFns,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nimport {\n  PaginationControls,\n  RowCount,\n  TableToolbar,\n} from './components/table-components'\nimport {\n  CategoryCell,\n  NumberCell,\n  PriceCell,\n  ProgressCell,\n  RowActionsCell,\n  StatusCell,\n  TextCell,\n} from './components/cell-components'\nimport {\n  ColumnFilter,\n  FooterColumnId,\n  FooterSum,\n  SortIndicator,\n} from './components/header-components'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel(),\n  paginatedRowModel: createPaginatedRowModel(),\n  sortFns,\n  filterFns,\n})\n\nexport const {\n  createAppColumnHelper,\n  injectAppTable,\n  injectTableContext,\n  injectTableCellContext,\n  injectTableHeaderContext,\n} = createTableHook({\n  features,\n  getRowId: (row) => row.id,\n  tableComponents: {\n    PaginationControls,\n    RowCount,\n    TableToolbar,\n  },\n  cellComponents: {\n    TextCell,\n    NumberCell,\n    ProgressCell,\n    StatusCell,\n    CategoryCell,\n    PriceCell,\n    RowActionsCell,\n  },\n  headerComponents: {\n    SortIndicator,\n    ColumnFilter,\n    FooterColumnId,\n    FooterSum,\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThis file is the source of truth for the feature set, row model pipeline, row IDs, and registered components used by both tables in the example.\n\n### Returned Helpers\n\n| Helper                     | Purpose                                                                                                                                 |\n| -------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `injectAppTable`           | Creates a table with the app's shared `features` (including row model factories), defaults, and registered components already attached. |\n| `createAppColumnHelper`    | Creates column helpers where `cell`, `header`, and `footer` contexts know about the registered components.                              |\n| `injectTableContext`       | Reads the current table inside registered table components like `PaginationControls`.                                                   |\n| `injectTableCellContext`   | Reads the current cell inside registered cell components like `TextCell`.                                                               |\n| `injectTableHeaderContext` | Reads the current header/footer inside registered header components like `SortIndicator`.                                               |\n\n### Component Columns\n\nUse `createAppColumnHelper<TData>()` instead of the base column helper when column definitions should render registered components.\n\n```ts\nimport { flexRenderComponent } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\nimport { createAppColumnHelper } from '../../table'\nimport type { Person } from '../../makeData'\n\nconst personColumnHelper = createAppColumnHelper<Person>()\n\nreadonly columns = personColumnHelper.columns([\n  personColumnHelper.accessor('firstName', {\n    header: 'First Name',\n    footer: ({ header }) => flexRenderComponent(header.FooterColumnId),\n    cell: ({ cell }) => flexRenderComponent(cell.TextCell),\n  }),\n  personColumnHelper.accessor('age', {\n    header: 'Age',\n    footer: ({ header }) => flexRenderComponent(header.FooterSum),\n    cell: ({ cell }) => flexRenderComponent(cell.NumberCell),\n  }),\n])\n```\n\nThe registered components are available through the enhanced `cell` and `header` objects because the column helper is bound to the `createTableHook` configuration.\n\n### Component Table Rendering\n\nCreate each table with `injectAppTable`. Per-table options provide the data and columns; shared features and row models come from `src/app/table.ts`.\n\n```ts\ntable = injectAppTable(() => ({\n  key: 'users-table',\n  columns: this.columns,\n  data: this.data(),\n  debugTable: true,\n}))\n```\n\nThe Angular table instance is augmented with:\n\n- `table.PaginationControls`, `table.RowCount`, and `table.TableToolbar`\n- `table.appCell(cell)` for enhanced cell component types in templates\n- `table.appHeader(header)` for enhanced header component types in templates\n- `table.appFooter(footer)` for enhanced footer component types in templates\n\nRegistered table components can access the table through Angular DI:\n\n```ts\nexport class PaginationControls {\n  readonly table = injectTableContext()\n}\n```\n\nIn templates, use the Angular rendering helpers with the app wrappers:\n\n```html\n@for (_header of headerGroup.headers; track _header.id) { @let header =\ntable.appHeader(_header);\n\n<th (click)=\"header.column.getToggleSortingHandler()?.($event)\">\n  <ng-container *flexRenderHeader=\"header; let value\">\n    {{ value }}\n  </ng-container>\n  <ng-container\n    *flexRender=\"header.SortIndicator; props: header.getContext(); let value\"\n  >\n    {{ value }}\n  </ng-container>\n</th>\n}\n```\n\n### Reusing The Component Registry\n\nThe example has separate Users and Products table components. Both import `createAppColumnHelper` and `injectAppTable` from `src/app/table.ts`, so they share sorting, filtering, pagination, row IDs, toolbar controls, cell renderers, and header/footer renderers while keeping their own data and columns.\n\nIf different product areas need incompatible defaults, create another `createTableHook` setup file and export a second set of app helpers from there.\n\n## When To Use This Pattern\n\nUse `createTableHook` when multiple tables should share features, row models, default options, or conventions. Use the standalone `injectTable` API for a one-off table. Add the component registry only when the app wants standardized reusable table UI pieces.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Composable Tables (createTableHook) Guide\n---\n\n`createTableHook` creates an app-specific table factory. Use it to define shared features, row models, and default table options once, then create each Angular table with the columns and data that are unique to that table.\n\nThe same API can also register reusable table, cell, and header components, but component registration is optional. Start with shared options and features first; add reusable components only when your app needs standardized table UI pieces.\n\n## Examples\n\n- [Basic App Table](../examples/basic-app-table) - Minimal `createTableHook` usage without the larger component registry.\n- [Composable Tables](../examples/composable-tables) - Richer Users and Products tables sharing `src/app/table.ts` and reusable components.\n\n## Start With Shared Features and Options\n\nCreate one app table hook and put the feature set, row models, and shared defaults there. This example makes sorting available to every table created by `injectAppTable`.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createTableHook,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortFns,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  sortFns,\n})\n\nconst { injectAppTable, createAppColumnHelper } = createTableHook({\n  features,\n  debugTable: true,\n  enableSortingRemoval: false,\n})\n```\n\nOptions passed to `createTableHook` become defaults for every table created by `injectAppTable`. The `features` option is also bound to the returned column helper, so column definitions know that sorting APIs are available.\n\n## Create App Columns\n\nCreate one column helper per row type. The helper is already bound to your app's feature set, so each table does not need to thread `typeof features` through its column definitions.\n\n```ts\ntype Person = {\n  firstName: string\n  lastName: string\n  age: number\n  visits: number\n}\n\nconst columnHelper = createAppColumnHelper<Person>()\n\nconst columns = columnHelper.columns([\n  columnHelper.accessor('firstName', {\n    cell: (info) => info.getValue(),\n  }),\n  columnHelper.accessor((row) => row.lastName, {\n    id: 'lastName',\n    header: () => 'Last Name',\n    cell: (info) => info.getValue(),\n  }),\n  columnHelper.accessor('age', {\n    header: 'Age',\n  }),\n  columnHelper.accessor('visits', {\n    header: 'Visits',\n  }),\n])\n```\n\n## Create A Table\n\nCreate each table with `injectAppTable`. The call site provides table-specific inputs such as `columns` and `data`; shared features and defaults come from the hook.\n\n```ts\nexport class UsersTable {\n  readonly data = signal<Array<Person>>([])\n\n  readonly table = injectAppTable(() => ({\n    key: 'users-table',\n    columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n  }))\n}\n```\n\n## Render With The Normal Table APIs\n\nYou can render the table with the same table instance APIs used by a standalone `injectTable` table. This simple path does not require `appCell`, `appHeader`, `appFooter`, or registered components.\n\n```html\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    @for (headerGroup of table.getHeaderGroups(); track headerGroup.id) {\n    <tr>\n      @for (header of headerGroup.headers; track header.id) {\n      <th (click)=\"header.column.getToggleSortingHandler()?.($event)\">\n        @if (!header.isPlaceholder) {\n        <ng-container *flexRenderHeader=\"header; let headerCell\">\n          {{ headerCell }}\n        </ng-container>\n        }\n      </th>\n      }\n    </tr>\n    }\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    @for (row of table.getRowModel().rows; track row.id) {\n    <tr>\n      @for (cell of row.getAllCells(); track cell.id) {\n      <td>\n        <ng-container *flexRenderCell=\"cell; let renderCell\">\n          {{ renderCell }}\n        </ng-container>\n      </td>\n      }\n    </tr>\n    }\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n```\n\n## Override Shared Defaults Per Table\n\nOptions passed to `injectAppTable` override defaults from `createTableHook`. Use this for the few tables that need different behavior without creating a separate app hook.\n\n```ts\nreadonly table = injectAppTable(() => ({\n  key: 'sortable-users-table',\n  columns,\n  data: this.data(),\n  enableSortingRemoval: true,\n}))\n```\n\n## Optional: Reusable Components\n\nThe richer composable-tables example also uses `createTableHook` as a component registry. Use this when several tables should share the same toolbar controls, cell renderers, header renderers, or footer renderers.\n\n### Component Registry Setup\n\nThe composable tables example keeps the shared setup in `src/app/table.ts`. That file creates one app-specific table factory and exports the helpers used by the rest of the example.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  createFilteredRowModel,\n  createPaginatedRowModel,\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createTableHook,\n  filterFns,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortFns,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nimport {\n  PaginationControls,\n  RowCount,\n  TableToolbar,\n} from './components/table-components'\nimport {\n  CategoryCell,\n  NumberCell,\n  PriceCell,\n  ProgressCell,\n  RowActionsCell,\n  StatusCell,\n  TextCell,\n} from './components/cell-components'\nimport {\n  ColumnFilter,\n  FooterColumnId,\n  FooterSum,\n  SortIndicator,\n} from './components/header-components'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel(),\n  paginatedRowModel: createPaginatedRowModel(),\n  sortFns,\n  filterFns,\n})\n\nexport const {\n  createAppColumnHelper,\n  injectAppTable,\n  injectTableContext,\n  injectTableCellContext,\n  injectTableHeaderContext,\n} = createTableHook({\n  features,\n  getRowId: (row) => row.id,\n  tableComponents: {\n    PaginationControls,\n    RowCount,\n    TableToolbar,\n  },\n  cellComponents: {\n    TextCell,\n    NumberCell,\n    ProgressCell,\n    StatusCell,\n    CategoryCell,\n    PriceCell,\n    RowActionsCell,\n  },\n  headerComponents: {\n    SortIndicator,\n    ColumnFilter,\n    FooterColumnId,\n    FooterSum,\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThis file is the source of truth for the feature set, row model pipeline, row IDs, and registered components used by both tables in the example.\n\n### Returned Helpers\n\n| Helper                     | Purpose                                                                                                                                 |\n| -------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `injectAppTable`           | Creates a table with the app's shared `features` (including row model factories), defaults, and registered components already attached. |\n| `createAppColumnHelper`    | Creates column helpers where `cell`, `header`, and `footer` contexts know about the registered components.                              |\n| `injectTableContext`       | Reads the current table inside registered table components like `PaginationControls`.                                                   |\n| `injectTableCellContext`   | Reads the current cell inside registered cell components like `TextCell`.                                                               |\n| `injectTableHeaderContext` | Reads the current header/footer inside registered header components like `SortIndicator`.                                               |\n\n### Component Columns\n\nUse `createAppColumnHelper<TData>()` instead of the base column helper when column definitions should render registered components.\n\n```ts\nimport { flexRenderComponent } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\nimport { createAppColumnHelper } from '../../table'\nimport type { Person } from '../../makeData'\n\nconst personColumnHelper = createAppColumnHelper<Person>()\n\nreadonly columns = personColumnHelper.columns([\n  personColumnHelper.accessor('firstName', {\n    header: 'First Name',\n    footer: ({ header }) => flexRenderComponent(header.FooterColumnId),\n    cell: ({ cell }) => flexRenderComponent(cell.TextCell),\n  }),\n  personColumnHelper.accessor('age', {\n    header: 'Age',\n    footer: ({ header }) => flexRenderComponent(header.FooterSum),\n    cell: ({ cell }) => flexRenderComponent(cell.NumberCell),\n  }),\n])\n```\n\nThe registered components are available through the enhanced `cell` and `header` objects because the column helper is bound to the `createTableHook` configuration.\n\n### Component Table Rendering\n\nCreate each table with `injectAppTable`. Per-table options provide the data and columns; shared features and row models come from `src/app/table.ts`.\n\n```ts\ntable = injectAppTable(() => ({\n  key: 'users-table',\n  columns: this.columns,\n  data: this.data(),\n  debugTable: true,\n}))\n```\n\nThe Angular table instance is augmented with:\n\n- `table.PaginationControls`, `table.RowCount`, and `table.TableToolbar`\n- `table.appCell(cell)` for enhanced cell component types in templates\n- `table.appHeader(header)` for enhanced header component types in templates\n- `table.appFooter(footer)` for enhanced footer component types in templates\n\nRegistered table components can access the table through Angular DI:\n\n```ts\nexport class PaginationControls {\n  readonly table = injectTableContext()\n}\n```\n\nIn templates, use the Angular rendering helpers with the app wrappers:\n\n```html\n@for (_header of headerGroup.headers; track _header.id) { @let header =\ntable.appHeader(_header);\n\n<th (click)=\"header.column.getToggleSortingHandler()?.($event)\">\n  <ng-container *flexRenderHeader=\"header; let value\">\n    {{ value }}\n  </ng-container>\n  <ng-container\n    *flexRender=\"header.SortIndicator; props: header.getContext(); let value\"\n  >\n    {{ value }}\n  </ng-container>\n</th>\n}\n```\n\n### Reusing The Component Registry\n\nThe example has separate Users and Products table components. Both import `createAppColumnHelper` and `injectAppTable` from `src/app/table.ts`, so they share sorting, filtering, pagination, row IDs, toolbar controls, cell renderers, and header/footer renderers while keeping their own data and columns.\n\nIf different product areas need incompatible defaults, create another `createTableHook` setup file and export a second set of app helpers from there.\n\n## When To Use This Pattern\n\nUse `createTableHook` when multiple tables should share features, row models, default options, or conventions. Use the standalone `injectTable` API for a one-off table. Add the component registry only when the app wants standardized reusable table UI pieces.\n"}
